[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to the [38;5;153m<main>[39m element in [38;5;153mindex.html[39m:

  [90m<[34mlabel[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m [36mname[90m=[31m"done"[90m>[39m
    Example task
  [90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m

  It's the browser's built-in checkbox. The browser handles the on/off state, so no JavaScript was needed. Wrapping it
  in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m means clicking the text also toggles it, and screen readers announce the text with the checkbox. I
  haven't opened the page in a browser to check it.

  The state isn't saved, so it resets when the page reloads. Change "Example task" to your own text, and copy the
  [38;5;153m<label>[39m block for each extra item.

  I didn't commit anything. Possible next steps, if you want them: strike through items when they're checked, save the
  state across reloads, or add a way to create new items.

